---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqLD = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is RealtyJuggler cheaper than BirkyStudio?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For a pure contact organizer, yes, and honestly it is hard to beat. RealtyJuggler is $179/year ($15/month) with the rate fixed for life and a pro-rated refund at any time. BirkyStudio is not really competing on that axis. If all you want is an affordable real estate CRM you run yourself, RealtyJuggler is excellent value. BirkyStudio costs more because you are buying a different thing: an AI operator that answers your phone, replies on WhatsApp, follows up automatically, and hands you verified prospects, not a database you have to work."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does RealtyJuggler answer my phone or reply to leads?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. RealtyJuggler is a CRM, not an AI agent. It stores your contacts, schedules your follow-up calls, and can send drip emails and letters, but you write and send those yourself. It has no AI voice receptionist and no AI text answering. BirkyStudio's Voice Receptionist is $550 one-time (plus Vapi usage of about $30-50/month) and answers calls 24/7 in English and Spanish. The Text Receptionist for WhatsApp is $297 one-time and holds full AI conversations."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does BirkyStudio include a CRM?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. The Notion CRM built for agents is included free with The Base Agent ($1,297 solo, from $2,997 for a team). So if you want both the AI operator and a place to store your contacts, you do not pay a separate CRM fee. What you give up versus RealtyJuggler is depth: RealtyJuggler has real estate specific tools like commission splits, rental management, printed flyers and letters, and seven mortgage calculators."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does RealtyJuggler find me leads?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. RealtyJuggler is a place to organize leads you already have. You import contacts from your MLS, tax records, or a third-party lead service, and it helps you work them. It does not supply leads. BirkyStudio's Verified Prospect List is a real, enriched, scored list of prospects built for your niche and area ($497 Starter, $997 Pro, one-time), and the $1,997 Lead Generation Pack adds outreach plus the AI that catches the replies."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does RealtyJuggler have a free trial or a contract?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "RealtyJuggler has the longest free trial in the category: 90 days, no credit card required, and any remaining trial time is added to your paid year. There is no contract. It is a $179/year membership, the price is fixed for life, and you can get a pro-rated refund at any time. That is genuinely customer-friendly. BirkyStudio matches the no-contract part with a 30-day money-back guarantee and no setup fee."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the difference between a CRM and an AI agent?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A CRM is where you store and organize contacts. It only does something when you sit down and work it. An AI agent acts on its own. BirkyStudio's Base Agent reads every website and WhatsApp enquiry, sorts it, saves it to the Notion CRM, answers it instantly, and follows up automatically in English and Spanish. The CRM holds the information. The AI agent is the one picking up the phone at 9pm while you are at dinner."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Who should choose RealtyJuggler over BirkyStudio?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "An agent or small team who wants an affordable, feature-deep real estate CRM they are happy to run themselves, who wants printed letters, commission tracking, rental tools, and seven mortgage calculators, and who likes included phone support and one-on-one training. RealtyJuggler is a genuinely great tool at $179/year. BirkyStudio is for agents who do not want to be the one doing all the work, and who want the phone answered and the follow-up handled without them."
      }
    }
  ]
});

const articleLD = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "BirkyStudio vs RealtyJuggler (2026 Comparison), Cheap CRM vs an Operator That Works",
  "description": "Honest head-to-head comparison of BirkyStudio vs RealtyJuggler for real estate agents. RealtyJuggler is a $179/year real estate CRM you run yourself. BirkyStudio is a done-for-you AI operator that answers your phone, replies on WhatsApp, follows up automatically, and hands you verified prospects. Real pricing, real pros and cons, no bias.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Luna Jerney",
    "url": "https://birkystudio.com"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Birky Studio",
    "url": "https://birkystudio.com"
  },
  "datePublished": "2026-09-29",
  "dateModified": "2026-09-29"
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BirkyStudio vs RealtyJuggler (2026)"
  description="BirkyStudio vs RealtyJuggler honest comparison for real estate agents. RealtyJuggler is a $179/year CRM you run yourself. BirkyStudio is a done-for-you AI operator that answers your phone, replies on WhatsApp and hands you verified prospects."
  image="/images/comparison/realtyjuggler.jpg"
  >
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLD} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={articleLD} />

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section style="padding:100px 0 80px;position:relative;overflow:hidden">
    <div style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 20% 50%,rgba(255,45,149,0.15),transparent 50%),radial-gradient(circle at 80% 50%,rgba(255,45,149,0.1),transparent 50%);"></div>
    <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px;position:relative;z-index:1;">
      <div style="display:inline-block;padding:8px 20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:100px;color:white;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:500;margin-bottom:20px;">
        Updated September 2026 • Honest comparison
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,3rem);font-weight:800;color:white;margin-bottom:20px;line-height:1.15;">
        BirkyStudio vs RealtyJuggler<br>
        <span style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--bs-accent),var(--bs-accent));-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;">A $179/year CRM vs an Operator That Works</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;max-width:700px;">
        RealtyJuggler is one of the most loved real estate CRMs there is: $179 a year, fixed for life, with included phone support and a 90-day free trial. It is a genuinely great contact organizer. BirkyStudio is not a contact organizer. We hand you an AI operator that answers your phone and WhatsApp 24/7 in English and Spanish, follows up automatically, and delivers verified prospects you own. One is a tool you sit down and work. The other works while you are out showing. Here is the honest breakdown.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <section style="padding:80px 0">
    <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px;">

      <!-- Quick Answer -->
      <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--bs-bg-raised),var(--bs-bg-raised));border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;border:1px solid rgba(255,45,149,0.3);">
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BirkyStudio if:</strong> You want the phone answered and the follow-up handled without you. You get an AI agent that replies to every enquiry in seconds, an AI receptionist on WhatsApp and voice, verified prospects you own, and a website you control. Best for solo agents and small teams who are drowning in admin, not short of contacts.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose RealtyJuggler if:</strong> You want an affordable, feature-deep real estate CRM you are happy to run yourself. $179 a year, fixed for life, with printed letters, commission tracking, rental tools, and seven mortgage calculators, all backed by included phone support and one-on-one training. Honestly, for a pure CRM, it is hard to beat.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">The honest difference:</strong> RealtyJuggler is software you operate. It only does something when you sit down and work it. BirkyStudio is an operator that does the work for you: it answers, it follows up, it qualifies, 24/7. If you only need somewhere to store contacts, buy RealtyJuggler. If you need the work done, that is a different job.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Image 1 -->
      <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <img src="/images/comparison/realtyjuggler-article-1.jpg" alt="Real estate agent writing notes in a planner beside a laptop at a bright modern desk while organizing client contacts" style="width:100%;max-width:800px;border-radius:12px;height:auto;box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);" loading="lazy">
      </div>

      <!-- Why Compare -->
      <h2 style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:16px;">Why compare BirkyStudio and RealtyJuggler?</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
        RealtyJuggler and BirkyStudio get compared because they both promise to reduce the admin that eats a real estate agent's day. RealtyJuggler is a real estate specific CRM built by Geeks on the Beach, running for over twenty years, with a 4.9 out of 5 average across 600+ Google reviews. It tracks prospects, generates daily call lists, prints letters and labels, sends drip emails, calculates commissions, and dials from your phone. All for $179 a year.
      </p>
      <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
        BirkyStudio takes a different route. Instead of giving you software to operate, we build and run an AI operator for you. The Base Agent reads every website and WhatsApp enquiry, sorts it, saves it to a Notion CRM built for agents, answers it instantly, and follows up automatically, in English and Spanish. Add the AI Receptionist and the phone is answered 24/7. Add the Verified Prospect List and you get real, enriched, scored prospects you own forever.
      </p>
      <p style="color:var(--bs-text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:40px;">
        Both are answering the same complaint: too much admin, too little selling. But they answer it differently. One hands you a better tool. The other takes the work off your desk. The difference shows up in what you pay, what you own, what you give up, and who does the work at 9pm on a Saturday. That is what this page breaks down.
      </p>

      <!-- Comparison Table -->
      <h2 id="comparison" style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:24px;">BirkyStudio vs RealtyJuggler. Side by Side</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin-bottom:64px;">
        <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="border-bottom:2px solid var(--bs-accent);">
              <th style="text-align:left;padding:14px 12px;color:var(--bs-accent);font-weight:600;">Feature</th>
              <th style="text-align:left;padding:14px 12px;color:var(--bs-accent);font-weight:600;">BirkyStudio</th>
              <th style="text-align:left;padding:14px 12px;color:var(--bs-accent);font-weight:600;">RealtyJuggler</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);">
